!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/class2/validate/valid/a-record-fields-type-may-be-a-dependent-type-expected.tn"
!!import:"https://tson.io/test-suite/schemas/validate-sidecar.tn"
{
  spec: "[TSON-SCHEMA] §4.2, [TSON-SCHEMA] §5.2, [TSON-SCHEMA] §8.1"
  description: """
    A schema read as data against the kernel: `record_field.type` is a `meta.type_expr`, a type's name or a type
    written in place, and a dependent type written in place, `{ of: !meta.dependent { on: kind } }`, is one, so the
    record is valid data. Whether `on` names a field declared before it is the schema's rule, judged where a schema
    resolves, not this read's.
    """
  valid: _
}
